; Next candidate for the first noun phrase
;
; One step of the search for what the first typed noun phrase (RecBuf1) means.
; The search position is the cursor RecPtr1 ($794E), which #R$7AA1 sets before
; the first call; every call goes on from where the last one stopped.
; .
; If Noun1Kind is NOUN_PLACE the candidates are the destinations of the exits
; of the actor's location whose names fit the phrase (#R$9EA0). Otherwise they
; are the objects whose names fit (#R$9DD9) and that are of the kind the
; command takes: AllMode ($B710) is set from bits 2-3 of StateB71E (0 things,
; 1 living characters, 2 anything). A candidate is accepted when the check of
; the command lets it through (#R$7CFC); the accepted one is left in
; FirstObject.
; .
; O:A Id of the accepted object or place, $FF when there are no more
; O:F Z when there are no more
; O:FirstObject The accepted candidate
; O:HL Destroyed (IY is preserved)
@label=NextNoun1
c$7CCB PUSH IY       ;
 $7CCD LD IX,($794E) ; RecPtr1: the cursor
 $7CD1 LD A,($B6FE)  ; Noun1Kind
 $7CD4 DEC A         ;
 $7CD5 JR Z,$7CF1    ; a place
 $7CD7 LD IY,$9DD9   ; FindNextNamedObject
 $7CDB LD A,($B71E)  ; StateB71E
 $7CDE RRCA          ;
 $7CDF RRCA          ;
 $7CE0 AND $03       ; noun 1 kind: bits 2-3
 $7CE2 LD ($B710),A  ; AllMode
 $7CE5 CALL $7CFC    ; NextNoun1Match
 $7CE8 CP $FF        ;
*$7CEA LD ($794E),IX ; RecPtr1
 $7CEE POP IY        ;
 $7CF0 RET           ;
@label=NextNoun1Place
*$7CF1 LD IY,$9EA0   ; FindExitByName
 $7CF5 CALL $7CFC    ; NextNoun1Match
 $7CF8 CP $FF        ;
 $7CFA JR $7CEA      ;
